      "text": "This is not just an analogy — bacteria literally implement\n  information processing in their regulatory circuits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OPERON = IF-THEN LOGIC:\n  lac operon: IF (lactose present AND glucose absent) THEN transcribe\n  trp operon: IF (tryptophan absent) THEN transcribe\n  These are genetic boolean circuits, formally equivalent to\n  digital logic gates operating on chemical concentrations."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TWO-COMPONENT SIGNALING = SENSOR + ACTUATOR:\n  Sensor kinase (membrane): Detects environmental signal\n  Response regulator: Changes gene expression\n  ~30+ two-component systems in E. coli → modular sensing network\n  Formally: sensor → ADC → register (response reg.) → output"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#011",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "QUORUM SENSING = DISTRIBUTED CONSENSUS:\n  Bacteria secrete autoinducers (AI)\n  Each cell monitors local [AI] concentration\n  When [AI] > threshold → all cells switch behavior simultaneously\n  Applications: Biofilm formation, virulence factor secretion\n  Formally: distributed threshold consensus algorithm in a\n            network of N identical agents (Valiant's work applies)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#012",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GENE REGULATORY NETWORK = BOOLEAN CIRCUIT:\n  Transcription factors (activators + repressors)\n  Build AND/OR/NOT gates from promoter architecture\n  Complex programs (sporulation, chemotaxis, SOS response)\n  all encoded as regulatory circuits in DNA\n```"
    },
