        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PRE-METAGENOMICS PROBLEM:\n  >99% of environmental bacteria cannot be cultured in a lab.\n  Classical microbiology (streak a plate, pick a colony) misses\n  almost everything."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#017",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "METAGENOMICS SOLUTION:\n  Extract DNA directly from environment (no culturing)\n  Sequence all DNA at once → computational assembly\n  Identify organisms from sequence alone"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#018",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:microbiology:00-overview, git-history:microbiology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "microbiology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:microbiology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "microbiology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "microbiology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microbiology - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "TWO APPROACHES:\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ 16S rRNA AMPLICON SEQUENCING                                 │\n  │   PCR amplify 16S rRNA gene (present in all bacteria)        │\n  │   Sequence amplicons → compare to database                   │\n  │   Identifies which bacteria are present (who's there?)       │\n  │   Cheap: ~$10–30/sample                                      │\n  │   Limitation: Semi-quantitative; primer bias; no function    │\n  │                                                              │\n  │ SHOTGUN METAGENOMICS                                         │\n  │   Sequence ALL DNA in sample (not just 16S)                  │\n  │   Reconstruct genomes: metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs)   │\n  │   Identifies: Who's there + What they can do (function)      │\n  │   Expensive: ~$100–500/sample                                │\n  │   Tools: Kraken2/Bracken (classify), MetaSPAdes (assembly)   │\n  │           MetaPhlAn4 (species profiling), HUMAnN3 (function) │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
