      },
      "text": "BIOGEOCHEMICAL CYCLES:\n  ─ Nitrogen fixation: ONLY bacteria + archaea can fix N₂ → NH₃\n    (All nitrogen in food web ultimately from microbial fixation)\n  ─ Oxygen in atmosphere: Cyanobacteria generated it (GOE, ~2.4 Ga)\n  ─ Carbon cycle: Decomposition (soil bacteria + fungi)\n  ─ Sulfur cycle: Sulfate-reducing bacteria in anaerobic sediments\n  ─ Without microbes: Most multicellular life impossible"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#024",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
